Section: Compile Flags

  CompileFlags = record {
   prose : Boolean,
   escape-check : Boolean,
   poison-compact : Boolean,
   deck-scale : Integer,
   phase-trace : Boolean,
   wire-trace : Boolean,
   pipeline : List Text
  }

  compile-flags-default : CompileFlags
  compile-flags-default = CompileFlags { prose = False, escape-check = False, poison-compact = False, deck-scale = 100, phase-trace = False, wire-trace = False, pipeline = default-ir-pipeline }

 A floor is a guard band plus a workspace, and only the workspace scales. The
 band is what the phase's write-path check reserves to stop short in, so a
 scaled floor that eats into it makes the guard fire on a deck holding almost
 nothing: measured 2026-08-03, a 1082-byte app refused at decks=11 with
 CDX9002 from DESUGAR, whose scaled floor was 7.92 MB against an 8 MB band,
 while the phase's real usage was 88 KB. That put a hard bottom on the knob at
 about 12 per cent for reasons unrelated to how much room anything needed.

 At pct 100 the branch evaluates the previous expression exactly, truncation
 included, so every reservation is unchanged at the shipping setting. The
 emitted binary does change, because this function gained a parameter; what
 is preserved is what it computes. Verified rather than argued: the same
 source measured under the seed and under the new compiler produces
 byte-identical deck origins across all seven decks.

  deck-min-workspace : Integer = 2097152

  scaled-floor : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scaled-floor (pct) (floor) (band) =
   if pct == 100 then floor / 100 * pct
   else let ws = (floor - band) / 100 * pct
    in band + (if ws < deck-min-workspace then deck-min-workspace else ws)

  deck-scale-of : Text -> Integer
  deck-scale-of (mode) =
   let v = mode-flag-value mode "decks=" 0
   in if v < 1 then 0 else v

 deck-scale-anchor is the compiler's own concatenated unit, measured 2026-08-04
 (`build/concat-codex-self.ps1 -CodexDir codex/compiler`). This said it is the
 length that maps to a scale of 100. It is not: deck-scale-margin doubles the
 estimate, so a unit of exactly this length derives 200 and is clamped, and the
 length that actually maps to 100 is HALF the anchor, 1,496,788. Everything
 above that gets the same reservation, so the derivation stops tracking length
 at half the anchor rather than at the anchor.

 Staleness is not safe in both directions either, though this said it was. The
 argument covered only the compiler growing. An anchor LARGER than the true
 unit divides every estimate down and hands the linear band less room, and that
 is the direction that happened: measured 2026-08-09 the unit is 2,746,259
 bytes, 247,317 below the anchor. It costs nothing today because the linear
 band holds 15 of 2814 measurable entry points and the other 2799 are at the
 floor or the clamp, neither of which the anchor touches.

 deck-scale-margin is headroom over the linear estimate, and 2 is measured
 rather than chosen for roundness. Across 29 units above 150 KB the binding
 phase is DESUGAR and the ratio of the linear estimate to the scale actually
 required ran from 1.24 to 1.71, so the bare estimate clears the requirement by
 as little as a quarter. Doubling it puts the tightest observed case at 2.5x.
 The reason margin is needed at all is that phase usage is NOT reliably linear
 in unit length below that size: CHECK usage per unit byte was measured between
 21x and 167x and is not monotonic, so a bare linear estimate is a line through
 points that do not lie on one.

 deck-scale-min is what 99 per cent of the corpus actually receives: measured
 2026-08-09 over every quire, 2798 of 2814 measurable entry points derive the
 floor, 15 derive from the linear term and 1 derives the clamp. So the floor is
 not a fallback, it IS the derivation, and the linear term between them governs
 fifteen units.

 It is set from density rather than from length, because density is where a
 length-derived scale fails. It was set from the two worst-density units known
 in 2026-08-04, and THOSE ARE NO LONGER THE BINDING CASE. Bisected 2026-08-09
 against seed A66E54F57CBAEBFD, the 46 units of the Shell quire (`codex/build`,
 70 to 102 KB each) need 34 to 43, the worst being `vmconfigScript`, which
 refuses at 42 and compiles at 43. `codex/test/shell-build-keep` needs 30. The
 Shell quire is what the floor must now clear, and 43 against 64 is 1.49x.
 Outside those 46 and the compiler, nothing in the tree is closer than 2.13x.

 The floor was 32, and at 32 a short deck fails BOTH ways. Measured 2026-08-05
 against seed 52E0A3A00218E19F, on `codex/build`, every unit of which derives
 the floor exactly:

 - **Silently.** `checkappsScript.codex` compiles clean at 32 and its output
   carries the intermediate states of a string concatenation, each with its
   length byte. At 33 and above it is byte-identical to the same unit at 150.
   Deterministic across three compiles, with a byte-identical CDX. This is the
   defect that was bisected to a seed change and read as a Text or rope fault.
   The seed is not at fault; the knob is.
 - **Loudly.** `BuildScript.codex`, `vmconfigScript.codex` and
   `comparecodexsemanticScript.codex` all refuse at 32 with `CDX9002: Deck
   overflow in CHECK` and compile at 64.

 The claim that certified 32 was that a sweep of all 1674 entry points at this
 setting raises no CDX9002. `BuildScript.codex` raises exactly that at 32, so
 the sweep's corpus did not cover the units that fail -- the Shell quire is not
 in the seed's reach and nothing gated compiles it. **A sweep cannot certify a
 floor for a quire it does not enumerate, and CDX9002 cannot certify one at
 all**, because the silent arm above raises nothing. Certify a floor by OUTPUT
 EQUALITY over a corpus that names its scope.

 64 was double the value known to break when it was chosen. It is 1.49x it now,
 because the Shell quire needs 43 and needed 33 four days earlier: measured
 2026-08-09, `checkappsScript` refuses at 34 and compiles at 36 where
 2026-08-05 recorded it byte-identical at 33. The compiler is not what moved.
 The same unit's CHECK deck usage is byte-identical under seeds
 AEB5ED2B5043C7C1, 065D92E60292492D and A66E54F57CBAEBFD, so the requirement is
 growing with the units and the floor is a constant that does not follow them.
 `build/deck-headroom.ps1` is the runner that re-measures this.

 The ceiling on the cost is that `derive-deck-scale` clamps at 100 and 100 is
 what every unit received before this derivation existed, so 64 cannot reserve
 more than the arrangement it replaced.

 The clamp is a ceiling on the CURE as well as on the cost, and one unit is
 already past it. `codex/test/apps/foreword-all-compile` needs at least 131:
 measured 2026-08-09 at decks=200 its LOWER deck uses 437,990,744 bytes, and
 -Measure runs no IR pipeline so the shipping LOWER is larger again. It
 compiles only because a `.flags` sidecar overrides the derivation with 200.
 At the 100 it would derive, the CDX path refuses with CDX9002 naming LOWER,
 which is the right answer, and the -Measure path faults in `bag-add` instead
 of raising, which is C2's open item reproduced on a real unit.

 **The mechanism this paragraph called unnamed is CHECK-KEEP, and `mc-sat` WAS
 it.** `mcopy-sat` read `let z = __record-set mc "mc-sat" 1 in x` and `MemoCtx`
 is not `mutable`, so the set built a record that was bound to `z` and
 discarded; the caller's `mc.mc-sat` was 0 on every path ever taken. When the
 keep frontier passes `mc-ceiling` the copy hands back the ORIGINAL pointer,
 which is scratch the caller reclaims a moment later, and the flag that was
 supposed to turn that into CDX9002 could not be set. A dangling `CodexType`
 then reaches `lookup-expr-type`, an append over it classifies as neither text
 nor list, and the program is miscompiled rather than refused. The flag is
 deleted and the caller now compares the keep deck's measured end against
 `mc-ceiling`, which is sound because the keep frontier is monotonic across
 these copies.

  deck-scale-anchor : Integer = 2993576
  deck-scale-margin : Integer = 2
  deck-scale-min : Integer = 64

  derive-deck-scale : Integer -> Integer
  derive-deck-scale (unit-len) =
   let est = unit-len * 100 * deck-scale-margin / deck-scale-anchor
   in if est < deck-scale-min then deck-scale-min
      else if est > 100 then 100
      else est

  effective-deck-scale : Text, Integer -> Integer
  effective-deck-scale (mode) (unit-len) =
   let explicit = deck-scale-of mode
   in if explicit > 0 then explicit else derive-deck-scale unit-len

  pipeline-of : Text -> List Text
  pipeline-of (mode) =
   let v = mode-flag-text mode "passes="
   in if v == "" then default-ir-pipeline
      else if v == "none" then []
      else if v == "text-plug" then text-plug-ir-pipeline
      else if text-starts-with v "+" then default-ir-pipeline & parse-pipeline-names (substring v 1 (text-length v - 1))
      else parse-pipeline-names v

  poison-lex : Integer = 161
  poison-parse : Integer = 162
  poison-desugar : Integer = 163
  poison-scope : Integer = 164
  poison-check : Integer = 165
  poison-lower : Integer = 166
  poison-resolve : Integer = 167
  poison-lift : Integer = 168
  poison-frontend : Integer = 169

  poison-phase-label : Integer -> Text
  poison-phase-label (byte) =
   if byte == 161 then "LEX"
   else if byte == 162 then "PARSE"
   else if byte == 163 then "DESUGAR"
   else if byte == 164 then "SCOPE"
   else if byte == 165 then "CHECK"
   else if byte == 166 then "LOWER"
   else if byte == 167 then "RESOLVE"
   else if byte == 168 then "LIFT"
   else if byte == 169 then "FRONTEND"
   else ""

  compact-phase : CompileFlags, Integer -> Nothing
  compact-phase (flags) (byte) =
   let marked = phase-trace-mark (flags.phase-trace) byte
   in if flags.poison-compact then phase-compact-poison byte
      else phase-compact

Section: Compile Target

  CompileTarget =
   | CtCodexText
   | CtX86_64Bare
   | CtCdx

Section: Frontend

  CompileFrontend = record {
   type-defs : List ATypeDef,
   text-meta : IRTextMeta,
   ir : IRChapter,
   cdx-ir : IRChapter,
   sorted-type-defs : List TypeBinding,
   renames : List RenameEntry,
   bag : DiagnosticBag,
   heap-marks : List Integer,
   phase-metrics : List PhaseMetrics
  }

  LexResult = record {
   tokens : List Token,
   bag : DiagnosticBag,
   heap-marks : List Integer,
   phase-metrics : List PhaseMetrics
  }

  ParseResult = record {
   doc : Document,
   colliding : SkipListText,
   assignments : List ChapterAssignment,
   chapter-names : List Text,
   parse-bag : DiagnosticBag,
   heap-marks : List Integer,
   phase-metrics : List PhaseMetrics
  }

  ScopeResult = record {
   scoped : AChapter,
   ctor-names : List Text,
   renames : List RenameEntry,
   colliding : SkipListText,
   assignments : List ChapterAssignment,
   resolve-bag : DiagnosticBag,
   heap-marks : List Integer,
   phase-metrics : List PhaseMetrics
  }

  CompileChecked = record {
   scoped : AChapter,
   all-bindings : List TypeBinding,
   ust : UnificationState,
   ctor-names : List Text,
   renames : List RenameEntry,
   colliding : SkipListText,
   assignments : List ChapterAssignment,
   bag : DiagnosticBag,
   heap-marks : List Integer,
   phase-metrics : List PhaseMetrics
  }

  halted-frontend : DiagnosticBag, List Integer -> CompileFrontend
  halted-frontend (bag) (marks) =
   let blank-name = Name { value = "" }
   in let blank-ir = IRChapter {
       name = blank-name,
       defs = [],
       effect-op-names = [],
       span = synthetic-span
      }
   in CompileFrontend {
    type-defs = [],
    text-meta = IRTextMeta { chapter-title = "", prose = "", section-titles = [], ctor-names = [], prose-blocks = [], annotations = [], ground-effects = [] },
    ir = blank-ir,
    cdx-ir = blank-ir,
    sorted-type-defs = [],
    renames = [],
    bag = bag,
    heap-marks = marks,
    phase-metrics = []
   }

  halted-checked : DiagnosticBag, List Integer -> CompileChecked
  halted-checked (bag) (marks) =
   CompileChecked {
    scoped = AChapter {
      name = Name { value = "" },
      defs = [],
      type-defs = [],
      effect-defs = [],
      class-defs = [],
      instance-defs = [],
      citations = [],
      ground-effects = [],
      chapter-title = "",
      prose = "",
      prose-blocks = [],
      annotations = [],
      section-titles = [],
      rt-names = [],
      rt-budgets = [],
      conversions = [],
      span = synthetic-span
    },
    all-bindings = [],
    ust = empty-unification-state,
    ctor-names = [],
    renames = [],
    colliding = skip-list-text-empty,
    assignments = [],
    bag = bag,
    heap-marks = marks,
    phase-metrics = []
   }

  check-deck-overflow : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  check-deck-overflow (usage) (budget) =
   if usage > budget then 1 else 0

  deck-overflow-bag : Text -> DiagnosticBag
  deck-overflow-bag (phase-name) =
   bag-from-list [make-error cdx-deck-overflow ("Deck overflow in " & phase-name & "; deck floor exceeded") synthetic-span]

  no-overflow-bag : DiagnosticBag = bag-from-list []

  serial-byte : Integer -> Integer
  serial-byte (b) = port-out-byte 1016 b

  serial-hex-digit : Integer -> Integer
  serial-hex-digit (d) =
   if d < 10 then serial-byte (48 + d)
   else serial-byte (87 + d)

  serial-hex-loop : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  serial-hex-loop (val) (shift) =
   if shift < 0 then 0
   else let d = bit-and (bit-shru val shift) 15
   in let w = serial-hex-digit d
   in serial-hex-loop val (shift - 4)

  serial-hex : Integer -> Integer
  serial-hex (val) = serial-hex-loop val 60

  serial-newline : Integer = serial-byte 10

  serial-text-loop : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  serial-text-loop (t) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then 0
   else let w = serial-byte (to-unicode (char-code (char-at t i)))
   in serial-text-loop t (i + 1) len

  serial-text : Text -> Integer
  serial-text (t) = serial-text-loop t 0 (text-length t)

  phase-trace-mark : Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  phase-trace-mark (on) (byte) =
   if on
    then let w = serial-text ("PH:" & poison-phase-label byte)
    in serial-newline
   else 0

  scan-deck-dangling : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scan-deck-dangling (addr) (deck-end) (bivy-lo) (bivy-hi) (count) =
   if addr >= deck-end then count
   else let val = peek-qword addr 0
   in if val >= bivy-lo
      then if val < bivy-hi
           then scan-deck-dangling (addr + 8) deck-end bivy-lo bivy-hi (count + 1)
           else scan-deck-dangling (addr + 8) deck-end bivy-lo bivy-hi count
      else scan-deck-dangling (addr + 8) deck-end bivy-lo bivy-hi count

  check-escape-invariant : PhaseMetrics, Text -> DiagnosticBag
  check-escape-invariant (m) (phase-name) =
   let violations = scan-deck-dangling (m.deck-origin) (m.deck-end) (m.bivy-origin) (m.bivy-hwm) 0
   in if violations > 0
      then bag-from-list [make-warning cdx-escape-violation ("Escape invariant: " & show violations & " deck pointer(s) target bivy in " & phase-name) synthetic-span]
      else bag-from-list []

  escape-check-bag : Boolean, PhaseMetrics, Text -> DiagnosticBag
  escape-check-bag (enabled) (m) (phase-name) =
   if enabled then check-escape-invariant m phase-name
   else bag-from-list []

  precise-escape-bag : Boolean, Integer, Text, PhaseMetrics, Text -> DiagnosticBag
  precise-escape-bag (enabled) (root-addr) (type-name) (m) (phase-name) =
   if enabled then
    let escaped = pmap-escape-count root-addr type-name (m.bivy-origin) (m.bivy-hwm)
    in let reached = pmap-escape-reached root-addr type-name
    in bag-from-list [make-warning cdx-escape-violation ("PRECISE escape (" & phase-name & "/" & type-name & "): " & show escaped & " ptr(s) into bivy, reach " & show reached) synthetic-span]
   else bag-from-list []

  pmap-selftest-bag : Boolean -> DiagnosticBag
  pmap-selftest-bag (enabled) =
   if enabled then pmap-selftest-result pmap-self-test
   else bag-from-list []

  deck-live-warn : Text, Text, Integer -> DiagnosticBag
  deck-live-warn (root-name) (seg) (n) =
   bag-from-list [make-warning cdx-escape-violation ("DECK-LIVE " & root-name & " -> " & seg & ": " & show n & " ref(s)") synthetic-span]

  sum-tylist-lens : List (List CodexType), Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sum-tylist-lens (ls) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else sum-tylist-lens ls (i + 1) len (acc + list-length (list-at ls i))

  sum-fieldlist-lens : List (List RecordField), Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sum-fieldlist-lens (ls) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else sum-fieldlist-lens ls (i + 1) len (acc + list-length (list-at ls i))

  sum-ctorlist-lens : List (List SumCtor), Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sum-ctorlist-lens (ls) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else sum-ctorlist-lens ls (i + 1) len (acc + list-length (list-at ls i))

  sum-labellist-lens : List (List EffectLabel), Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sum-labellist-lens (ls) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else sum-labellist-lens ls (i + 1) len (acc + list-length (list-at ls i))

  pmap-selftest-result : Integer -> DiagnosticBag
  pmap-selftest-result (r) =
   if r == 3 then bag-from-list []
   else bag-from-list [make-warning cdx-escape-violation ("pmap-walk self-test FAILED: got " & show r & " (expect 3)") synthetic-span]

  compile-lex : Text, Integer, CompileFlags -> LexResult
  compile-lex (source) (h0) (flags) =
   let mountain-base = init-phase-allocator
   in let lex-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-lex-floor demand-lex-guard-band
   in let lex-base = build lex-deck-height
   in let lex-phase = phase-start
   in let tok-result = tokenize-into source 1 (flags.prose) (lex-base + lex-deck-height)
   in let tokens = tok-result.tokens
   in let lex-errors = tok-result.errors
   in let lex-bag = deck-record (bag-from-list lex-errors)
   in if bag-has-errors lex-bag
      then LexResult { tokens = [], bag = lex-bag, heap-marks = [h0], phase-metrics = [] }
      else let lex-metrics = phase-measure lex-phase "LEX"
   in let lex-ov = check-deck-overflow (lex-metrics.deck-end - lex-metrics.deck-origin) lex-deck-height
   in let lex-ov-bag = if lex-ov == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "LEX" else no-overflow-bag
   in let lex-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) lex-metrics "LEX"
   in let lex-bag2 = deck-record (bag-merge-all [lex-bag, lex-ov-bag, lex-esc-bag])
   in let result = deck-record (LexResult { tokens = tokens, bag = lex-bag2, heap-marks = [h0], phase-metrics = [lex-metrics] })
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-lex
   in result

  compile-parse : List Token, Text, Integer, List PhaseMetrics, CompileFlags -> ParseResult
  compile-parse (tokens) (source) (h0) (prior-metrics) (flags) =
   let h1 = __heap-save
   in let parse-keep-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-parse-keep-floor demand-parse-guard-band
   in let parse-base = build parse-keep-height
   in let parse-guard = pitch demand-parse-guard-band
   in let parse-scratch-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-parse-scratch-floor demand-parse-scratch-guard-band
   in let scratch-base = build (parse-scratch-height + (if parse-guard < 0 then 1 else 0))
   in let scratch-ceiling = scratch-base + parse-scratch-height
   in let parse-phase = phase-start
   in let st = make-parse-state tokens source
   in let scan = scan-document st
   in let h2 = __heap-save
   in let assignments-s = if deck-short-of scratch-ceiling demand-parse-scratch-guard-band then [] else deck-record (build-all-assignments source (scan.def-headers) 0 [])
   in let colliding-s = if deck-short-of scratch-ceiling demand-parse-scratch-guard-band then skip-list-text-empty else deck-record (find-colliding-names assignments-s)
   in let h3 = __heap-save
   in let entry-dup-bag = bag-from-list (check-entry-point-duplicate assignments-s)
   in let bset = deck-record (skip-list-text-from-list builtin-names)
   in let shadow-bag = bag-from-list (check-shadowed-builtins (scan.def-headers) bset 0 (list-length (scan.def-headers)) [])
   in let collide-bag = bag-from-list (check-cross-chapter-collisions (scan.def-headers) colliding-s assignments-s 0 (list-length (scan.def-headers)) [])
   in let doc = parse-document (make-parse-state tokens source) scratch-ceiling
   in let prose-diags = if flags.prose then check-prose-consistency doc & check-prose-banned doc else []
   in let h4 = __heap-save
   in let parse-sat = if deck-short-of scratch-ceiling demand-parse-scratch-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let parse-bag = deck-record (bag-merge-all [doc.parse-bag, entry-dup-bag, shadow-bag, collide-bag, bag-from-list prose-diags])
   in if bag-has-errors parse-bag
      then ParseResult { doc = doc, colliding = colliding-s, assignments = assignments-s, chapter-names = scan.chapter-names, parse-bag = parse-bag, heap-marks = [h0, h1, h2, h3, h4], phase-metrics = prior-metrics }
      else let parse-metrics = phase-measure parse-phase "PARSE"
   in let parse-ov = check-deck-overflow (parse-metrics.deck-end - parse-metrics.deck-origin) parse-scratch-height
   in let dset-keep = __deck-set parse-base
   in let keep-phase = phase-start
   in let gcopy = deck-record (copy-sx-document-guarded parse-base (parse-base + parse-keep-height) doc)
   in let doc2 = gcopy.doc
   in let assignments = deck-record (for a in assignments-s -> deck-record (ChapterAssignment { def-name = copy-sx-text parse-base (a.def-name), chapter-slug = copy-sx-text parse-base (a.chapter-slug) }))
   in let chapter-names-k = deck-record (copy-sx-texts parse-base (scan.chapter-names))
   in let colliding-names = skip-list-text-to-list colliding-s
   in let colliding = deck-record (skip-list-text-from-list (copy-sx-texts parse-base colliding-names))
   in let parse-bag-d = deck-record (copy-sx-bag parse-base parse-bag)
   in let keep-metrics = phase-measure keep-phase "PARSE-KEEP"
   in let keep-ov = check-deck-overflow (keep-metrics.deck-end - keep-metrics.deck-origin) parse-keep-height
   in let parse-metrics-d = deck-record (PhaseMetrics {
    label = parse-metrics.label,
    bivy-origin = parse-metrics.bivy-origin,
    bivy-hwm = parse-metrics.bivy-hwm,
    deck-origin = parse-metrics.deck-origin,
    deck-end = parse-metrics.deck-end
   })
   in let scratch-top = if parse-metrics.deck-end > parse-metrics.bivy-hwm then parse-metrics.deck-end else parse-metrics.bivy-hwm
   in let keep-esc-metrics = PhaseMetrics {
    label = keep-metrics.label,
    bivy-origin = parse-metrics.deck-origin,
    bivy-hwm = scratch-top,
    deck-origin = keep-metrics.deck-origin,
    deck-end = keep-metrics.deck-end
   }
   in let keep-esc-bag = deck-record (escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) keep-esc-metrics "PARSE")
   in let parse-precise-bag = deck-record (precise-escape-bag (flags.escape-check) (address-of doc2) "Document" keep-esc-metrics "PARSE")
   in let parse-ov-bag = if parse-ov == 1 | parse-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "PARSE" else no-overflow-bag
   in let keep-ov-bag = if keep-ov == 1 | gcopy.sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "PARSE-KEEP" else no-overflow-bag
   in let parse-bag2 = deck-record (bag-merge-all [parse-bag-d, parse-ov-bag, keep-ov-bag, keep-esc-bag, parse-precise-bag])
   in let keep-metrics-d = deck-record (PhaseMetrics {
    label = keep-metrics.label,
    bivy-origin = keep-metrics.bivy-origin,
    bivy-hwm = keep-metrics.bivy-hwm,
    deck-origin = keep-metrics.deck-origin,
    deck-end = keep-metrics.deck-end
   })
   in let parse-phase-metrics = deck-record (list-push (list-push prior-metrics parse-metrics-d) keep-metrics-d)
   in let result = deck-record (ParseResult { doc = doc2, colliding = colliding, assignments = assignments, chapter-names = chapter-names-k, parse-bag = parse-bag2, heap-marks = [h0, h1, h2, h3, h4], phase-metrics = parse-phase-metrics })
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-parse
   in result

  compile-desugar-and-scope : Text, ParseResult, Text, CompileFlags, Integer, Integer -> ScopeResult
  compile-desugar-and-scope (source) (pr) (chapter-name) (flags) (fk-base) (fk-height) =
   let desugar-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-desugar-floor demand-desugar-guard-band
   in let desugar-base = build desugar-deck-height
   in let desugar-phase = phase-start
   in let dr = desugar-document source (pr.doc) chapter-name (desugar-base + desugar-deck-height)
   in let ast = dr.dr-chapter
   in let desugar-metrics = phase-measure desugar-phase "DESUGAR"
   in let desugar-ov = check-deck-overflow (desugar-metrics.deck-end - desugar-metrics.deck-origin) desugar-deck-height
   in let dset-keep = __deck-set fk-base
   in let keep-phase = phase-start
   in let fk-ceiling = fk-base + fk-height - demand-frontend-keep-guard-band
   in let fkcopy = deck-record (copy-as-chapter-guarded fk-base fk-ceiling ast)
   in let ast2 = fkcopy.chapter
   in let assignments = deck-record (for a in (pr.assignments) -> deck-record (ChapterAssignment { def-name = copy-sx-text fk-base (a.def-name), chapter-slug = copy-sx-text fk-base (a.chapter-slug) }))
   in let chapter-names = deck-record (copy-sx-texts fk-base (pr.chapter-names))
   in let colliding-names = skip-list-text-to-list (pr.colliding)
   in let colliding = deck-record (skip-list-text-from-list (copy-sx-texts fk-base colliding-names))
   in let parse-bag-d = deck-record (copy-sx-bag fk-base (pr.parse-bag))
   in let heap-marks-d = deck-record (for h in (pr.heap-marks) -> h)
   in let desugar-metrics-d = deck-record (PhaseMetrics { label = desugar-metrics.label, bivy-origin = desugar-metrics.bivy-origin, bivy-hwm = desugar-metrics.bivy-hwm, deck-origin = desugar-metrics.deck-origin, deck-end = desugar-metrics.deck-end })
   in let phase-metrics-d = deck-record (for m in (pr.phase-metrics) -> deck-record (PhaseMetrics { label = m.label, bivy-origin = m.bivy-origin, bivy-hwm = m.bivy-hwm, deck-origin = m.deck-origin, deck-end = m.deck-end }))
   in let keep-metrics = phase-measure keep-phase "DESUGAR-KEEP"
   in let keep-ov = check-deck-overflow (keep-metrics.deck-end - keep-metrics.deck-origin) fk-height
   in let desugar-ov-bag = deck-record (if desugar-ov == 1 | dr.dr-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "DESUGAR" else no-overflow-bag)
   in let keep-ov-bag = deck-record (if keep-ov == 1 | fkcopy.sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "DESUGAR-KEEP" else no-overflow-bag)
   in let desugar-esc-bag = deck-record (escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) desugar-metrics "DESUGAR")
   in let desugar-sealed = compact-phase flags poison-desugar
   in let h5 = __heap-save
   in let scope-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-scope-floor demand-scope-guard-band
   in let scope-base = build scope-deck-height
   in let scope-ceiling = scope-base + scope-deck-height
   in let scope-origin = __deck-pos
   in let scope-phase = phase-start
   in let scoped = scope-achapter ast2 colliding assignments scope-ceiling
   in let h6 = __heap-save
   in let cite-bag = deck-record (check-duplicate-cites (scoped.citations))
   in let missing-cite-bag = deck-record (check-cites-resolve (scoped.citations) assignments chapter-names)
   in let resolve-result = resolve-chapter scoped colliding assignments scope-ceiling
   in let resolve-bag = deck-record (bag-merge-all [parse-bag-d, cite-bag, missing-cite-bag, resolve-result.bag, desugar-ov-bag, keep-ov-bag, desugar-esc-bag, pmap-selftest-bag True])
   in let scope-end = __deck-pos
   in let scope-sat = if deck-short-of scope-ceiling demand-scope-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let scope-metrics = phase-measure scope-phase "SCOPE"
   in let scope-ov = check-deck-overflow (scope-end - scope-origin) scope-deck-height
   in let scope-ov-bag = if scope-ov == 1 | scope-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "SCOPE" else no-overflow-bag
   in let scope-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) scope-metrics "SCOPE"
   in let scope-precise-bag = precise-escape-bag (flags.escape-check) (address-of scoped) "AChapter" scope-metrics "SCOPE"
   in let resolve-bag2 = deck-record (bag-merge-all [resolve-bag, scope-ov-bag, scope-esc-bag, scope-precise-bag])
   in let hm1 = deck-record (list-push heap-marks-d h5)
   in let scope-heap-marks = deck-record (list-push hm1 h6)
   in let pm1 = deck-record (list-push phase-metrics-d desugar-metrics-d)
   in let scope-phase-metrics = deck-record (list-push pm1 scope-metrics)
   in let global-renames = deck-record (build-global-rename-table assignments colliding)
   in let result = deck-record (ScopeResult {
    scoped = scoped,
    ctor-names = resolve-result.ctor-names,
    renames = global-renames,
    colliding = colliding,
    assignments = assignments,
    resolve-bag = resolve-bag2,
    heap-marks = scope-heap-marks,
    phase-metrics = scope-phase-metrics
   })
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-scope
   in result

 The CHECK deck is measured TWICE and the two are not redundant. `check-metrics`
 is taken before the resolve tail because `memo-graph` sizes the memo table from
 it, so moving it later makes that sizing depend on itself. `CHECK-RESOLVE` is
 the same deck at its true end, after `resolved-env`, `sorted-all0` and
 `sorted-et0`, which are the deck-recorded allocations `post-ov-bag` exists to
 catch. Reading CHECK's requirement off the first number understates it by 7 to
 29 per cent, measured over four units 2026-08-09.

  compile-type-check : ScopeResult, Integer, CompileFlags -> CompileChecked
  compile-type-check (sr) (source-len) (flags) =
   let check-units = count-typecheck-units (sr.scoped.type-defs) 0 (list-length (sr.scoped.type-defs)) 0
   in let check-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-check-floor demand-check-guard-band
   in let keep-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-check-keep-floor 0
   in let keep-base = build keep-height
   in let check-base = build check-deck-height
   in let check-ceiling = check-base + check-deck-height
   in let check-origin = __deck-pos
   in let check-phase = phase-start
   in let check-result = deck-record (check-chapter (sr.scoped) (sr.renames) (sr.colliding) (sr.assignments) check-ceiling)
   in let h8 = __heap-save
   in let cap-diags = deck-record (check-opening-capabilities (check-result.types))
   in let check-bag0 = deck-record (bag-merge-all [sr.resolve-bag, check-result.state.bag, bag-from-list cap-diags])
   in let check-end = __deck-pos
   in let check-sat = if deck-short-of check-ceiling demand-check-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let check-metrics = phase-measure check-phase "CHECK"
   in let check-ov = check-deck-overflow (check-end - check-origin) check-deck-height
   in let check-ov-bag = if check-ov == 1 | check-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "CHECK" else no-overflow-bag
   in let check-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) check-metrics "CHECK"
   in let check-bag = deck-record (bag-merge-all [check-bag0, check-ov-bag, check-esc-bag])
   in let check-heap-marks = deck-record (list-push (sr.heap-marks) h8)
   in let check-phase-metrics = deck-record (list-push (sr.phase-metrics) check-metrics)
   in if bag-has-errors check-bag
      then halted-checked check-bag check-heap-marks
      else let resolved-env = deck-record (for b in (check-result.env.bindings) -> deck-record (TypeBinding { name = b.name, bound-type = deep-resolve (check-result.state) (b.bound-type) }))
      in let sorted-all0 = deck-record (resolve-all-bindings (check-result.state) (sort-bindings (check-result.types & resolved-env)) 0 (list-length (check-result.types) + list-length resolved-env) (__list-with-capacity (list-length (check-result.types) + list-length resolved-env)))
      in let sorted-et0 = deck-record (resolve-all-expr-types (check-result.state) (sort-expr-types (check-result.state.expr-types)) 0 (list-length (check-result.state.expr-types)) (__list-with-capacity (list-length (check-result.state.expr-types))))
      in let post-ov-bag = if __deck-pos > check-ceiling then deck-overflow-bag "CHECK" else no-overflow-bag
      in let memo-pop0 = list-length sorted-et0 * 32 + list-length sorted-all0 * 32 + 1024
      in let memo-graph = (check-metrics.deck-end - check-metrics.deck-origin) / 64
      in let memo-pop = if memo-graph > memo-pop0 then memo-graph else memo-pop0
      in let memo-slots = memo-pow2-at-least (memo-pop * 2) 4096
      in let memo-table = pitch (memo-slots * 8)
      in let memo-z = __memset memo-table 0 (memo-slots * 8)
      in let cons-slots = memo-pow2-at-least (memo-pop / 2) 4096
      in let cons-table = pitch (cons-slots * 16)
      in let cons-z = __memset cons-table 0 (cons-slots * 16)
      in let mc = MemoCtx {
       mc-table = memo-table,
       mc-slots = memo-slots,
       mc-shift = memo-shift-for memo-slots 64,
       mc-floor = keep-base,
       mc-ty = __list-with-capacity memo-pop,
       mc-text = __list-with-capacity memo-pop,
       mc-name = __list-with-capacity (memo-pop / 2 + 16),
       mc-row = __list-with-capacity (memo-pop / 16 + 16),
       mc-tylist = __list-with-capacity (memo-pop / 4 + 16),
       mc-fieldlist = __list-with-capacity (memo-pop / 4 + 16),
       mc-ctorlist = __list-with-capacity (memo-pop / 4 + 16),
       mc-labellist = __list-with-capacity (memo-pop / 4 + 16),
       mc-cons = cons-table,
       mc-cons-slots = cons-slots,
       mc-cons-shift = memo-shift-for cons-slots 64,
       mc-cap-ty = memo-pop,
       mc-cap-text = memo-pop,
       mc-cap-name = memo-pop / 2 + 16,
       mc-cap-row = memo-pop / 16 + 16,
       mc-cap-list = memo-pop / 4 + 16,
       mc-ceiling = keep-base + keep-height - 4194304
      }
      in let check-resolve-metrics = phase-measure check-phase "CHECK-RESOLVE"
      in let all-phase-metrics = deck-record (list-push check-phase-metrics check-resolve-metrics)
      in let keep-set = __deck-set keep-base
      in let keep-phase = phase-start
      in let sorted-all = deck-record (copy-bindings-deep sorted-all0 mc)
      in let sorted-et = deck-record (copy-expr-types-deep sorted-et0 mc)
      in let kept-subs = deck-record (mcopy-types (check-result.state.substitutions) 0 mc)
      in let kept-rows = deck-record (mcopy-rows (check-result.state.row-substitutions) mc)
      in let kept-bag = deck-record (copy-sx-bag keep-base check-bag)
      in let kept-ust-bag = deck-record (copy-sx-bag keep-base (check-result.state.bag))
      in let kept-marks = deck-record (copy-list-with-headroom check-heap-marks 0)
      in let kept-metrics = deck-record (for m in all-phase-metrics -> deck-record (PhaseMetrics { label = m.label, bivy-origin = m.bivy-origin, bivy-hwm = m.bivy-hwm, deck-origin = m.deck-origin, deck-end = m.deck-end }))
      in let keep-metrics = phase-measure keep-phase "CHECK-KEEP"
      in let keep-ov = check-deck-overflow (keep-metrics.deck-end - keep-metrics.deck-origin) keep-height
      in let keep-ov-bag = if keep-ov == 1 | keep-metrics.deck-end >= mc.mc-ceiling then deck-overflow-bag "CHECK-KEEP" else no-overflow-bag
      in let keep-stat-bag = if flags.escape-check then deck-record (bag-from-list [make-warning cdx-escape-violation ("KEEP-STAT used=" & show (keep-metrics.deck-end - keep-metrics.deck-origin) & " ty=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-ty)) & " text=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-text)) & " name=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-name)) & " row=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-row)) & " tylists=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-tylist)) & "/" & show (sum-tylist-lens (mc.mc-tylist) 0 (list-length (mc.mc-tylist)) 0) & " fieldlists=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-fieldlist)) & "/" & show (sum-fieldlist-lens (mc.mc-fieldlist) 0 (list-length (mc.mc-fieldlist)) 0) & " ctorlists=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-ctorlist)) & "/" & show (sum-ctorlist-lens (mc.mc-ctorlist) 0 (list-length (mc.mc-ctorlist)) 0) & " labellists=" & show (list-length (mc.mc-labellist)) & "/" & show (sum-labellist-lens (mc.mc-labellist) 0 (list-length (mc.mc-labellist)) 0) & " subs=" & show (list-length kept-subs) & " et=" & show (list-length sorted-et) & " binds=" & show (list-length sorted-all)) synthetic-span]) else bag-from-list []
      in let final-bag = deck-record (bag-merge-all [kept-bag, keep-ov-bag, keep-stat-bag, post-ov-bag])
      in let pre-sorted-ust = deck-record (UnificationState {
       substitutions = kept-subs,
       row-substitutions = kept-rows,
       next-id = check-result.state.next-id,
       next-row-id = check-result.state.next-row-id,
       bag = kept-ust-bag,
       expr-types = sorted-et,
       effect-exempt = False,
       scope-grants = [],
       chapter-grounds = []
      })
      in let result0 = deck-record (CompileChecked {
       scoped = sr.scoped,
       all-bindings = sorted-all,
       ust = pre-sorted-ust,
       ctor-names = sr.ctor-names,
       renames = sr.renames,
       colliding = sr.colliding,
       assignments = sr.assignments,
       bag = final-bag,
       heap-marks = kept-marks,
       phase-metrics = kept-metrics
      })
      in let check-scratch-top = if check-metrics.deck-end > check-metrics.bivy-hwm then check-metrics.deck-end else check-metrics.bivy-hwm
      in let check-esc-metrics = PhaseMetrics {
       label = keep-metrics.label,
       bivy-origin = check-metrics.deck-origin,
       bivy-hwm = check-scratch-top,
       deck-origin = keep-metrics.deck-origin,
       deck-end = keep-metrics.deck-end
      }
      in let check-precise-bag = deck-record (precise-escape-bag (flags.escape-check) (address-of result0) "CompileChecked" check-esc-metrics "CHECK")
      in let result = __record-set result0 "bag" (deck-record (bag-merge-all [final-bag, check-precise-bag]))
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-check
   in result

  compile-checked : Text, Text, CompileFlags -> CompileChecked
  compile-checked (source) (chapter-name) (flags) =
   let fk-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-frontend-keep-floor demand-frontend-keep-guard-band
   in let fk-base = build fk-height
   in let h0 = __heap-save
   in let lr = compile-lex source h0 flags
   in if bag-has-errors (lr.bag)
      then halted-checked (lr.bag) (lr.heap-marks)
      else let pr = compile-parse (lr.tokens) source h0 (lr.phase-metrics) flags
   in if bag-has-errors (pr.parse-bag)
      then halted-checked (pr.parse-bag) (pr.heap-marks)
      else let sr = compile-desugar-and-scope source pr chapter-name flags fk-base fk-height
   in if bag-has-errors (sr.resolve-bag)
      then halted-checked (sr.resolve-bag) (sr.heap-marks)
      else compile-type-check sr (text-length source) flags

  compile-frontend : Text, Text, CompileFlags -> CompileFrontend
  compile-frontend (source) (chapter-name) (flags) =
   compile-frontend-passes source chapter-name flags False

  compile-frontend-ir : Text, Text, CompileFlags -> CompileFrontend
  compile-frontend-ir (source) (chapter-name) (flags) =
   compile-frontend-passes source chapter-name flags True

  frontend-bag-with-passes : DiagnosticBag, DiagnosticBag, DiagnosticBag, DiagnosticBag, IRPassResult -> DiagnosticBag
  frontend-bag-with-passes (base) (ov) (esc) (precise) (passed) =
   bag-merge-all [base, ov, esc, precise,
     deck-record (ir-check-violation-bag (passed.violations)),
     deck-record (occ-info-bag (passed.infos))]

  compile-frontend-passes : Text, Text, CompileFlags, Boolean -> CompileFrontend
  compile-frontend-passes (source) (chapter-name) (flags) (run-passes) =
   let checked = compile-checked source chapter-name flags
   in if bag-has-errors (checked.bag) then halted-frontend (checked.bag) (checked.heap-marks)
   else let lower-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-lower-floor demand-lower-guard-band
   in let lower-base = build lower-deck-height
   in let lower-ceiling = lower-base + lower-deck-height
   in let lower-origin = __deck-pos
   in let lower-phase = phase-start
   in let ir-raw = deck-record (lower-chapter (checked.scoped) (checked.all-bindings) (checked.ust) (checked.ctor-names) (checked.renames) (checked.colliding) (checked.assignments) lower-ceiling)
   in let passed = if run-passes then deck-record (run-ir-pipeline (flags.pipeline) ir-raw (flags.phase-trace))
      else IRPassResult { chapter = ir-raw, violations = [], infos = [] }
   in let ir = passed.chapter
   in let tm = deck-record (IRTextMeta {
    chapter-title = checked.scoped.chapter-title,
    prose = checked.scoped.prose,
    section-titles = checked.scoped.section-titles,
    ctor-names = checked.ctor-names,
    prose-blocks = checked.scoped.prose-blocks,
    annotations = checked.scoped.annotations,
    ground-effects = checked.scoped.ground-effects
   })
   in let lower-end = __deck-pos
   in let lower-sat = if deck-short-of lower-ceiling demand-lower-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let lower-metrics = phase-measure lower-phase "LOWER"
   in let lower-ov = check-deck-overflow (lower-end - lower-origin) lower-deck-height
   in let lower-precise-bag = deck-record (precise-escape-bag (flags.escape-check) (address-of ir) "IRChapter" lower-metrics "LOWER")
   in let blank-ir = IRChapter { name = ir.name, defs = [], effect-op-names = ir.effect-op-names, span = ir.span }
   in let pm1 = deck-record (list-push (checked.phase-metrics) lower-metrics)
   in let lower-ov-bag = if lower-ov == 1 | lower-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "LOWER" else no-overflow-bag
   in let lower-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) lower-metrics "LOWER"
   in let fe-bag = deck-record (frontend-bag-with-passes (checked.bag) lower-ov-bag lower-esc-bag lower-precise-bag passed)
   in let lower-sealed = compact-phase flags poison-lower
   in let result = deck-record (CompileFrontend {
    type-defs = checked.scoped.type-defs,
    text-meta = tm,
    ir = ir,
    cdx-ir = blank-ir,
    sorted-type-defs = [],
    renames = checked.renames,
    bag = fe-bag,
    heap-marks = checked.heap-marks,
    phase-metrics = pm1
   })
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-frontend
   in result

  compile-frontend-cdx : Text, Text, CompileFlags -> CompileFrontend
  compile-frontend-cdx (source) (chapter-name) (flags) =
   let checked = compile-checked source chapter-name flags
   in if bag-has-errors (checked.bag) then halted-frontend (checked.bag) (checked.heap-marks)
   else let lower-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-lower-floor demand-lower-guard-band
   in let lower-base = build lower-deck-height
   in let lower-ceiling = lower-base + lower-deck-height
   in let lower-origin = __deck-pos
   in let lower-phase = phase-start
   in let ir-raw = deck-record (lower-chapter (checked.scoped) (checked.all-bindings) (checked.ust) (checked.ctor-names) (checked.renames) (checked.colliding) (checked.assignments) lower-ceiling)
   in let passed = deck-record (run-ir-pipeline (flags.pipeline) ir-raw (flags.phase-trace))
   in let ir = passed.chapter
   in let ir-check-bag = deck-record (ir-check-violation-bag (passed.violations))
   in let occ-report-bag = deck-record (occ-info-bag (passed.infos))
   in let lower-end = __deck-pos
   in let lower-sat = if deck-short-of lower-ceiling demand-lower-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let lower-metrics = phase-measure lower-phase "LOWER"
   in let lower-ov = check-deck-overflow (lower-end - lower-origin) lower-deck-height
   in let lower-precise-bag = deck-record (precise-escape-bag (flags.escape-check) (address-of ir) "IRChapter" lower-metrics "LOWER")
   in let lower-sealed = compact-phase flags poison-lower
   in let resolve-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-resolve-floor demand-resolve-guard-band
   in let resolve-base = build resolve-deck-height
   in let resolve-ceiling = resolve-base + resolve-deck-height
   in let resolve-phase = phase-start
   in let type-map = deck-record (build-type-def-map (checked.scoped.type-defs) 0 (list-length (checked.scoped.type-defs)) [])
   in let stds = deck-record (sort-bindings (type-map & checked.all-bindings))
   in let resolved-defs = deck-record (rewrite-ir-defs stds (ir.defs) resolve-ceiling)
   in let resolve-sat = if deck-short-of resolve-ceiling demand-resolve-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let resolve-metrics = phase-measure resolve-phase "RESOLVE"
   in let resolve-ov = check-deck-overflow (resolve-metrics.deck-end - resolve-metrics.deck-origin) resolve-deck-height
   in let lift-deck-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-lift-floor demand-lift-guard-band
   in let lift-base = build lift-deck-height
   in let lift-ceiling = lift-base + lift-deck-height
   in let lift-phase = phase-start
   in let cdx-chapter = deck-record (lift-lambdas (IRChapter {
    name = ir.name,
    defs = resolved-defs,
    effect-op-names = ir.effect-op-names,
    span = ir.span
   }) lift-ceiling)
   in let lift-sat = if deck-short-of lift-ceiling demand-lift-guard-band then 1 else 0
   in let lift-metrics = phase-measure lift-phase "LIFT"
   in let lift-ov = check-deck-overflow (lift-metrics.deck-end - lift-metrics.deck-origin) lift-deck-height
   in let tm = deck-record (IRTextMeta {
    chapter-title = checked.scoped.chapter-title,
    prose = checked.scoped.prose,
    section-titles = checked.scoped.section-titles,
    ctor-names = checked.ctor-names,
    prose-blocks = checked.scoped.prose-blocks,
    annotations = checked.scoped.annotations,
    ground-effects = checked.scoped.ground-effects
   })
   in let blank-ir = IRChapter { name = ir.name, defs = [], effect-op-names = ir.effect-op-names, span = ir.span }
   in let pm1 = deck-record (list-push (checked.phase-metrics) lower-metrics)
   in let pm2 = deck-record (list-push pm1 resolve-metrics)
   in let pm3 = deck-record (list-push pm2 lift-metrics)
   in let lower-ov-bag = if lower-ov == 1 | lower-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "LOWER" else no-overflow-bag
   in let resolve-ov-bag = if resolve-ov == 1 | resolve-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "RESOLVE" else no-overflow-bag
   in let lift-ov-bag = if lift-ov == 1 | lift-sat == 1 then deck-overflow-bag "LIFT" else no-overflow-bag
   in let lower-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) lower-metrics "LOWER"
   in let resolve-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) resolve-metrics "RESOLVE"
   in let lift-esc-bag = escape-check-bag (flags.escape-check) lift-metrics "LIFT"
   in let dl-bag = if flags.escape-check then
       if list-length (checked.phase-metrics) >= 5 then
        let m-lex = list-at (checked.phase-metrics) 0
        in let m-scope = list-at (checked.phase-metrics) 3
        in let m-check = list-at (checked.phase-metrics) 4
        in let ir-root = address-of cdx-chapter
        in let stds-root = address-of stds
        in deck-record (bag-merge-all [
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "pre-scope" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (m-lex.deck-origin) (m-scope.deck-origin)),
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "scope" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (m-scope.deck-origin) (m-scope.deck-end)),
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "check" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (m-check.deck-origin) (m-check.deck-end)),
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "lower" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (lower-metrics.deck-origin) (lower-metrics.deck-end)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "pre-scope" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (m-lex.deck-origin) (m-scope.deck-origin)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "scope" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (m-scope.deck-origin) (m-scope.deck-end)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "check" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (m-check.deck-origin) (m-check.deck-end)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "lower" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (lower-metrics.deck-origin) (lower-metrics.deck-end)),
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "scope-scratch" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (m-scope.deck-end) (m-scope.bivy-hwm)),
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "check-scratch" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (m-check.deck-end) (m-check.bivy-hwm)),
         deck-live-warn "cdx-ir" "lower-scratch" (pmap-escape-count-quiet ir-root "IRChapter" (lower-metrics.deck-end) (lower-metrics.bivy-hwm)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "scope-scratch" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (m-scope.deck-end) (m-scope.bivy-hwm)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "check-scratch" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (m-check.deck-end) (m-check.bivy-hwm)),
         deck-live-warn "stds" "lower-scratch" (pmap-escape-list-quiet stds-root "TypeBinding" (lower-metrics.deck-end) (lower-metrics.bivy-hwm))])
       else bag-from-list []
      else bag-from-list []
   in let lir-report-bag = deck-record (occ-info-bag (lir-report-if lir-target-x86 (flags.pipeline) cdx-chapter))
   in let lir-probe-bag = deck-record (occ-info-bag (lir-alloc-probe-if lir-target-a64-shape "A64" "lir-dump-a64" (flags.pipeline) cdx-chapter))
   in let lir-narrow-bag = deck-record (occ-info-bag (lir-alloc-probe-if lir-target-narrow-shape "NARROW" "lir-dump-a64" (flags.pipeline) cdx-chapter))
   in let fe-bag = deck-record (bag-merge-all [checked.bag, ir-check-bag, occ-report-bag, lir-report-bag, lir-probe-bag, lir-narrow-bag, lower-ov-bag, resolve-ov-bag, lift-ov-bag, lower-esc-bag, resolve-esc-bag, lift-esc-bag, lower-precise-bag, dl-bag])
   in let result = deck-record (CompileFrontend {
    type-defs = checked.scoped.type-defs,
    text-meta = tm,
    ir = blank-ir,
    cdx-ir = cdx-chapter,
    sorted-type-defs = stds,
    renames = checked.renames,
    bag = fe-bag,
    heap-marks = checked.heap-marks,
    phase-metrics = pm3
   })
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-frontend
   in result

Section: Library Loading

  is-library-quire : Text -> Boolean
  is-library-quire (q) =
   if q == "Foreword" then True
   else if q == "Kernel" then True
   else if q == "OS" then True
   else if q == "Works" then True
   else if q == "Trust" then True
   else if q == "Net" then True
   else if q == "Verify" then True
   else if q == "Replay" then True
   else if q == "Sched" then True
   else if q == "Observe" then True
   else if q == "Game" then True
   else if q == "Signal" then True
   else if q == "Compress" then True
   else if q == "Encode" then True
   else if q == "Math" then True
   else if q == "Sim" then True
   else if q == "AI" then True
   else if q == "UI" then True
   else if q == "Punctual" then True
   else if q == "Dev" then True
   else False

  quire-to-dir : Text -> Text
  quire-to-dir (q) =
   if q == "Foreword" then "foreword/"
   else if q == "Kernel" then "kernel/"
   else if q == "OS" then "os/"
   else if q == "Works" then "works/"
   else if q == "Trust" then "os.trust/"
   else if q == "Net" then "os.net/"
   else if q == "Verify" then "os.verify/"
   else if q == "Replay" then "os.replay/"
   else if q == "Sched" then "os.sched/"
   else if q == "Observe" then "os.observe/"
   else if q == "Game" then "foreword.game/"
   else if q == "Signal" then "foreword.signal/"
   else if q == "Compress" then "foreword.compress/"
   else if q == "Encode" then "foreword.encode/"
   else if q == "Math" then "foreword.math/"
   else if q == "Sim" then "foreword.sim/"
   else if q == "AI" then "foreword.ai/"
   else if q == "UI" then "foreword.ui/"
   else if q == "Punctual" then "foreword.punctual/"
   else if q == "Dev" then "os.dev/"
   else "foreword/"

  filter-library-cites : List CitesDecl, Integer, Integer, List CitesDecl -> List CitesDecl
  filter-library-cites (citations) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else let c = list-at citations i
   in if is-library-quire (token-text (c.quire))
      then filter-library-cites citations (i + 1) len (list-push acc c)
      else filter-library-cites citations (i + 1) len acc

Section: Disk Foreword Loading

  DiskLoadState = record {
   dls-seen : List Text,
   dls-chunks : List Text
  }

  disk-extract-cites : Text, Integer -> List CitesDecl
  disk-extract-cites (source) (ceiling) =
   let tok-result = tokenize-into source 1 False ceiling
   in let doc = parse-document (make-parse-state (tok-result.tokens) source) ceiling
   in filter-library-cites (doc.citations) 0 (list-length (doc.citations)) []

  disk-load-cite : Fat16Volume, DiskLoadState, Text, Text, Integer -> DiskLoadState
  disk-load-cite (vol) (st) (quire) (name) (ceiling) =
   let key = quire & ":" & name
   in if text-set-has (st.dls-seen) key then st
   else let seen2 = text-set-insert (st.dls-seen) key
   in let path = quire-to-dir quire & name & ".codex"
   in when fat16-read-text vol path
     is Just (content) ->
       let deps = disk-extract-cites content ceiling
       in let st2 = disk-load-cites-list vol (DiskLoadState { dls-seen = seen2, dls-chunks = st.dls-chunks }) deps 0 (list-length deps) ceiling
       in let renamed = text-replace content ("Chapter: " & name) ("Chapter: " & quire & "--" & name)
       in DiskLoadState { dls-seen = st2.dls-seen, dls-chunks = list-push (st2.dls-chunks) (renamed & "\n\n") }
     is None -> DiskLoadState { dls-seen = seen2, dls-chunks = st.dls-chunks }

  disk-load-cites-list : Fat16Volume, DiskLoadState, List CitesDecl, Integer, Integer, Integer -> DiskLoadState
  disk-load-cites-list (vol) (st) (cite-list) (i) (len) (ceiling) =
   if i >= len then st
   else let c = list-at cite-list i
   in let st2 = disk-load-cite vol st (token-text (c.quire)) (c.chapter-name) ceiling
   in disk-load-cites-list vol st2 cite-list (i + 1) len ceiling

  disk-resolve-forewords : Fat16Volume, Text, Text -> Text
  disk-resolve-forewords (vol) (source) (mode) =
   let scan-scale = effective-deck-scale mode (text-length source)
   in let scan-height = scaled-floor scan-scale demand-disk-scan-floor demand-disk-scan-guard-band
   in let scan-base = build scan-height
   in let ceiling = scan-base + scan-height
   in let cite-list = disk-extract-cites source ceiling
   in let st = disk-load-cites-list vol (DiskLoadState { dls-seen = [], dls-chunks = [] }) cite-list 0 (list-length cite-list) ceiling
   in let joined = deck-record (text-concat-list (st.dls-chunks))
   in let compacted = phase-compact
   in joined

Section: Quoted Works

 Threat model: the transport is untrusted. Whoever hands us these bytes
 may hand us anything at all, so the gate takes the messenger's word for
 nothing -- content that does not match its digest, a signer the source
 did not pin, a forged signature, and a score below the floor are each
 refused independently.

 The offered-works wire format, after the marker line: a KEY line per
 trusted key, giving its fingerprint, its public key in hex, and the
 score; and a WORK line per offered definition, giving its digest, its
 author, its timestamp, the fingerprint that signed it, the signature in
 hex, and the number of lines of content that follow.

  quoted-works-marker : Text = "%%QUOTED-WORKS%%"

  SourceSplit = record {
   sp-body : Text,
   sp-works : Text
  }

  match-at : Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  match-at (t) (m) (i) (j) (mlen) =
   if j >= mlen then True
   else if char-code-at t (i + j) /= char-code-at m j then False
   else match-at t m i (j + 1) mlen

  index-of-from : Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  index-of-from (t) (m) (i) (tlen) (mlen) =
   if i + mlen > tlen then -1
   else if match-at t m i 0 mlen then i
   else index-of-from t m (i + 1) tlen mlen

 The source is CCE by the time it reaches here, and CCE is not ASCII: a
 newline is 1, a space is 2, and 10 is the digit seven. A guard written
 against the ASCII numbers asks whether the character before the marker
 is a seven, decides it is not, and hands the offered works to the parser
 as if they were code. Ask the encoding for its own numbers. Never write
 them down.

  at-line-start : Text, Integer -> Boolean
  at-line-start (t) (i) =
   if i == 0 then True else char-code-at t (i - 1) == char-code '\n'

  at-line-end : Text, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  at-line-end (t) (i) (tlen) =
   if i >= tlen then True else char-code-at t i == char-code '\n'

  marker-line-at : Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  marker-line-at (src) (from) (tlen) (mlen) =
   let at = index-of-from src quoted-works-marker from tlen mlen
   in if at < 0 then -1
      else if at-line-start src at & at-line-end src (at + mlen) tlen then at
      else marker-line-at src (at + 1) tlen mlen

  split-quoted-works : Text -> SourceSplit
  split-quoted-works (src) =
   let tlen = text-length src
   in let mlen = text-length quoted-works-marker
   in let at = marker-line-at src 0 tlen mlen
   in if at < 0
      then SourceSplit { sp-body = src, sp-works = "" }
      else SourceSplit {
        sp-body = substring src 0 at,
        sp-works = substring src (at + mlen) (tlen - at - mlen)
      }

  next-line-at : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  next-line-at (t) (i) (tlen) =
   if i >= tlen then tlen
   else if char-code-at t i == char-code '\n' then i + 1
   else next-line-at t (i + 1) tlen

  line-opens-quotes : Text, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  line-opens-quotes (t) (i) (tlen) =
   if i >= tlen then False
   else if char-code-at t i == char-code ' ' then line-opens-quotes t (i + 1) tlen
   else if i + 7 > tlen then False
   else if match-at t "quotes" i 0 6 then char-code-at t (i + 6) == char-code ' '
   else False

  scan-for-quotes : Text, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  scan-for-quotes (t) (i) (tlen) =
   if i >= tlen then False
   else if line-opens-quotes t i tlen then True
   else scan-for-quotes t (next-line-at t i tlen) tlen

  has-quotations : Text -> Boolean
  has-quotations (body) = scan-for-quotes body 0 (text-length body)

Section: Hex

 The digits are contiguous in CCE and the letters are not: CCE orders
 them by frequency, so a is 15 and f is 28, and everything from o to w
 sits between them. A hex decoder written as two range checks over ASCII
 therefore accepts a dozen letters that are not hex digits and mis-values
 every one of them.

  hex-to-bytes : Text, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  hex-to-bytes (t) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i + 1 >= len then acc
   else let hi = hex-digit-value (char-code-at t i)
   in let lo = hex-digit-value (char-code-at t (i + 1))
   in hex-to-bytes t (i + 2) len (list-push acc (hi * 16 + lo))

  decode-hex : Text -> List Integer
  decode-hex (t) = hex-to-bytes t 0 (text-length t) []

Section: Reading The Offered Works

  WorksState = record {
   ws-bundle : FactBundle,
   ws-manifest : TrustManifest
  }

  works-empty : WorksState = WorksState { ws-bundle = bundle-empty, ws-manifest = manifest-empty }

  join-work-lines : List Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  join-work-lines (lines) (i) (stop) (acc) =
   if i >= stop then acc
   else join-work-lines lines (i + 1) stop (acc & list-at lines i & "\n")

 The trust manifest is built from the SOURCE, never from the offered works.
 A KEY line in the works blob is ignored on purpose: it arrives over the
 transport, and the transport is what the gate must not believe. A signer
 the source did not pin is an unknown signer, whatever the works claim.

  build-source-manifest : List CitesDecl, Integer, Integer, TrustManifest -> TrustManifest
  build-source-manifest (ks) (i) (len) (m) =
   if i >= len then m
   else let k = list-at ks i
   in let pub = decode-hex (k.content-hash)
   in let m2 = manifest-add m (k.chapter-name) pub (k.trust-floor)
   in build-source-manifest ks (i + 1) len m2

  parse-works : List Text, Integer, Integer, WorksState -> WorksState
  parse-works (lines) (i) (len) (st) =
   if i >= len then st
   else let ln = list-at lines i
   in if text-starts-with ln "KEY " then parse-works lines (i + 1) len st
      else if text-starts-with ln "WORK " then apply-work-line lines i len st
      else if text-starts-with ln "OFFER " then apply-offer-line lines i len st
      else parse-works lines (i + 1) len st

  apply-offer-line : List Text, Integer, Integer, WorksState -> WorksState
  apply-offer-line (lines) (i) (len) (st) =
   let f = text-split (list-at lines i) " "
   in if list-length f < 5 then parse-works lines (i + 1) len st
   else let nlines = text-to-integer (list-at f 4)
   in let content = join-work-lines lines (i + 1) (i + 1 + nlines) ""
   in let ts = text-to-integer (list-at f 3)
   in let fact = Fact { hash = list-at f 1, kind = DefinitionFact, content = content, author = list-at f 2, timestamp = ts }
   in let st2 = __record-set st "ws-bundle" (bundle-offer (st.ws-bundle) fact)
   in parse-works lines (i + 1 + nlines) len st2

  apply-work-line : List Text, Integer, Integer, WorksState -> WorksState
  apply-work-line (lines) (i) (len) (st) =
   let f = text-split (list-at lines i) " "
   in if list-length f < 7 then parse-works lines (i + 1) len st
   else let nlines = text-to-integer (list-at f 6)
   in let content = join-work-lines lines (i + 1) (i + 1 + nlines) ""
   in let ts = text-to-integer (list-at f 3)
   in let fact = Fact { hash = list-at f 1, kind = DefinitionFact, content = content, author = list-at f 2, timestamp = ts }
   in let sf = SignedFact { fact = fact, signature = decode-hex (list-at f 5), signer-fingerprint = list-at f 4 }
   in let st2 = __record-set st "ws-bundle" (bundle-publish (st.ws-bundle) sf)
   in parse-works lines (i + 1 + nlines) len st2

 No carriage return survives to be stripped here. CCE has no code point
 for one -- 13 is not in the table -- so the conversion at the I/O
 boundary drops it, and a CRLF file and an LF file are the same text by
 the time the gate sees them.

  build-works : Text -> WorksState
  build-works (works) =
   let lines = text-split works "\n"
   in parse-works lines 0 (list-length lines) works-empty

Section: Refusing A Quotation

  quotation-code : ImportOutcome -> Integer
  quotation-code (o) = when o
   is ImportOk (f) -> 0
   is ImportMissing -> cdx-quotation-missing
   is ImportCorrupt -> cdx-quotation-corrupt
   is ImportUnsigned -> cdx-quotation-unsigned
   is ImportUnknownSigner -> cdx-quotation-unknown-signer
   is ImportForged -> cdx-quotation-forged
   is ImportUntrusted (score) -> cdx-quotation-untrusted

  quotation-message : CitesDecl, ImportOutcome -> Text
  quotation-message (q) (o) = when o
   is ImportOk (f) -> ""
   is ImportMissing -> "Quoted work '" & q.chapter-name & "' was not supplied; nothing offered has hash " & q.content-hash
   is ImportCorrupt -> "Quoted work '" & q.chapter-name & "' does not hash to " & q.content-hash
   is ImportUnsigned -> "Quoted work '" & q.chapter-name & "' carries no signature; a hash says what a definition is, only a signature says who stands behind it"
   is ImportUnknownSigner -> "Quoted work '" & q.chapter-name & "' is signed by a key that is not in the trust manifest"
   is ImportForged -> "Quoted work '" & q.chapter-name & "' has a signature that does not verify against its signer's key"
   is ImportUntrusted (score) -> quotation-untrusted-message q score

  quotation-untrusted-message : CitesDecl, Integer -> Text
  quotation-untrusted-message (q) (score) =
   "Quoted work '" & q.chapter-name & "' is signed by a key scoring " & show score & ", below the floor of " & show (q.trust-floor)

  quotation-diag : CitesDecl, ImportOutcome -> Diagnostic
  quotation-diag (q) (o) =
   let sp = span-at (q.quire.line) (q.quire.column) (q.quire.offset) (q.quire.length) (q.quire.file-id)
   in make-error (__narrow (quotation-code o)) (quotation-message q o) sp

  quotation-no-floor-diag : CitesDecl -> Diagnostic
  quotation-no-floor-diag (q) =
   let sp = span-at (q.quire.line) (q.quire.column) (q.quire.offset) (q.quire.length) (q.quire.file-id)
   in make-error cdx-quotation-no-floor ("Chapter '" & q.citing-chapter & "' quotes a work but declares no trust floor; write 'trusting above N' (0 to 10000) to say how much trust a quoted work's signer must clear") sp

  QuoteResolve = record {
   qr-prefix : Text,
   qr-bag : DiagnosticBag
  }

 A quotation names its digest with the algorithm that produced it, so
 that the day we outgrow SHA-256 the old quotations still say what they
 meant. The store is keyed by the digest alone.

  digest-of : Text -> Text
  digest-of (h) =
   if text-starts-with h "sha256:" then substring h 7 (text-length h - 7) else h

  resolve-each : List CitesDecl, Integer, Integer, WorksState, Text, DiagnosticBag -> QuoteResolve
  resolve-each (qs) (i) (len) (ws) (prefix) (bag) =
   if i >= len then QuoteResolve { qr-prefix = prefix, qr-bag = bag }
   else let q = list-at qs i
   in let r = gate-import (ws.ws-bundle) (ws.ws-manifest) (q.trust-floor) (digest-of (q.content-hash)) (q.chapter-name)
   in when r.outcome
    is ImportOk (f) -> resolve-admit qs i len ws prefix bag q (f.content)
    is otherwise -> resolve-each qs (i + 1) len ws prefix (bag-add bag (quotation-diag q (r.outcome)))

  resolve-admit : List CitesDecl, Integer, Integer, WorksState, Text, DiagnosticBag, CitesDecl, Text -> QuoteResolve
  resolve-admit (qs) (i) (len) (ws) (prefix) (bag) (q) (content) =
   let renamed = rewrite-chapter-header content (q.chapter-name)
   in resolve-each qs (i + 1) len ws (prefix & renamed & "\n\n") bag

  line-end-at : Text, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  line-end-at (t) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then len
   else if char-code-at t i == char-code '\n' then i
   else line-end-at t (i + 1) len

  rewrite-chapter-header : Text, Text -> Text
  rewrite-chapter-header (content) (local-name) =
   let len = text-length content
   in let nl = line-end-at content 0 len
   in let head = substring content 0 nl
   in if text-starts-with head "Chapter:"
      then "Chapter: " & local-name & substring content nl (len - nl)
      else content

  resolve-quotations : Text, FactBundle -> QuoteResolve
  resolve-quotations (body) (bundle) =
   let tok-result = tokenize body 1
   in let doc = parse-document (make-parse-state (tok-result.tokens) body) 0
   in let qs = doc.quotations
   in if list-length qs == 0 then QuoteResolve { qr-prefix = "", qr-bag = empty-bag }
   else let q0 = list-at qs 0
   in if q0.trust-floor < 0
      then QuoteResolve { qr-prefix = "", qr-bag = bag-add empty-bag (quotation-no-floor-diag q0) }
   else let ks = doc.trust-keys
   in let manifest = build-source-manifest ks 0 (list-length ks) manifest-empty
   in let ws = WorksState { ws-bundle = bundle, ws-manifest = manifest }
   in resolve-each qs 0 (list-length qs) ws "" empty-bag

Section: Text Compilation

  compile-text : CompileFrontend, CompileTarget -> Text
  compile-text (fe) (target) =
   if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then ""
   else emit-for-text-target target (fe.ir) (fe.text-meta) (fe.type-defs) (fe.renames)

  emit-for-text-target : CompileTarget, IRChapter, IRTextMeta, List ATypeDef, List RenameEntry -> Text
  emit-for-text-target (target) (ir) (meta) (type-defs) (renames) =
   when target
    is CtCodexText -> codex-emit-text-chapter ir meta type-defs renames
    is CtX86_64Bare | CtCdx -> ""

Section: Binary Compilation

  compile-to-cdx : CompileFrontend -> EmitChapterResult
  compile-to-cdx (fe) = compile-to-cdx-with-exit-mode fe Exit False WatchdogProgress

  cdx-emit-roots : List Text
  cdx-emit-roots = ["opening", "fat16-servicer-read", "fat16-servicer-write"]

  compile-to-cdx-with-exit-mode : CompileFrontend, X86_64ExitMode, Boolean, X86_64WatchdogMode -> EmitChapterResult
  compile-to-cdx-with-exit-mode (fe) (exit-mode) (poison) (wd-mode) =
   if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then EmitChapterResult { header-bytes = [], content-buf = 0, content-len = 0, tail-bytes = [], bag = fe.bag, symbol-map = [] }
   else let all-defs = (fe.cdx-ir).defs
    in let proofs = keep-proof-defs [] all-defs 0
    in let pruned = ir-prune-unreachable-roots (fe.cdx-ir) cdx-emit-roots
    in let dropped = ir-dropped-budgeted-punctuals all-defs (pruned.defs)
    in let emit-result = x86-64-emit-cdx-with-exit-mode (ir-chapter-with-proofs pruned proofs) (fe.sorted-type-defs) exit-mode poison False wd-mode dropped
    in EmitChapterResult {
     header-bytes = emit-result.header-bytes,
     content-buf = emit-result.content-buf,
     content-len = emit-result.content-len,
     tail-bytes = emit-result.tail-bytes,
     bag = bag-merge-all [fe.bag, emit-result.bag],
     symbol-map = emit-result.symbol-map
    }

Section: Measurement

  phase-labels : List Text
  phase-labels =
   ["h0-start", "h1-tokenize", "h2-scan", "h3-assignments",
    "h4-parse", "h5-desugar", "h6-scope", "h7-resolve",
    "h8-check", "h9-lower", "h10-ctors",
    "h-pre-emit", "h-post-emit"]

  phase-metric-names : List Text
  phase-metric-names = ["lex", "parse", "desugar", "scope", "check", "lower", "resolve", "lift"]

  format-phase-metrics-wd : List PhaseMetrics -> Text
  format-phase-metrics-wd (metrics) =
   format-phase-metrics-loop metrics phase-metric-names 0 (list-length metrics) ""

  format-phase-metrics-loop : List PhaseMetrics, List Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  format-phase-metrics-loop (metrics) (names) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else let m = list-at metrics i
   in let name = if i < list-length names then list-at names i else "?"
   in let deck-usage = m.deck-end - m.deck-origin
   in let bivy-usage = m.bivy-hwm - m.bivy-origin
   in let line = "WD:PM-" & name & ":deck-origin=" & integer-to-text (m.deck-origin) & ",deck-end=" & integer-to-text (m.deck-end) & ",deck-usage=" & integer-to-text deck-usage & ",bivy-hwm=" & integer-to-text (m.bivy-hwm) & ",bivy-usage=" & integer-to-text bivy-usage & "\n"
   in format-phase-metrics-loop metrics names (i + 1) len (acc & line)

  format-heap-marks : List Integer -> Text
  format-heap-marks (marks) =
   text-concat-list (format-heap-marks-prefix marks phase-labels "PHASE-" 0 (list-length marks) [])

  format-heap-marks-wd : List Integer -> Text
  format-heap-marks-wd (marks) =
   text-concat-list (format-heap-marks-prefix marks phase-labels "WD:PHASE-" 0 (list-length marks) [])

  emit-mark-labels : List Text
  emit-mark-labels = ["h-pre-emit", "h-post-emit"]

  format-emit-marks : Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  format-emit-marks (pre) (post) (pfx) =
   text-concat-list (format-heap-marks-prefix [pre, post] emit-mark-labels pfx 0 2 [])

  format-heap-marks-prefix : List Integer, List Text, Text, Integer, Integer, List Text -> List Text
  format-heap-marks-prefix (marks) (labels) (pfx) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else let label = if i < list-length labels then list-at labels i else "h?"
    in format-heap-marks-prefix marks labels pfx (i + 1) len (list-push acc (pfx & label & ":" & integer-to-text (list-at marks i) & "\n"))

Section: Expr-Type Pre-Resolution

  resolve-all-expr-types : UnificationState, List ExprTypeEntry, Integer, Integer, List ExprTypeEntry -> List ExprTypeEntry
  resolve-all-expr-types (st) (entries) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else let e = list-at entries i
   in let resolved = deck-record (ExprTypeEntry { key = e.key, ty = deep-resolve st (e.ty) })
   in resolve-all-expr-types st entries (i + 1) len (list-push acc resolved)

  resolve-all-bindings : UnificationState, List TypeBinding, Integer, Integer, List TypeBinding -> List TypeBinding
  resolve-all-bindings (st) (bindings) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i >= len then acc
   else let b = list-at bindings i
   in let resolved = deck-record (TypeBinding { name = b.name, bound-type = deep-resolve st (b.bound-type) })
   in resolve-all-bindings st bindings (i + 1) len (list-push acc resolved)

Section: Codegen Diagnostics

  print-codegen-errors : List Diagnostic, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  print-codegen-errors (errs) (i) (len) =
   if i == len then print-line-uni ""
   else act
    print-line-uni (diagnostic-display (list-at errs i) empty-file-table)
    print-codegen-errors errs (i + 1) len
   end

  print-codegen-error-header : List Diagnostic -> [Console] Nothing
  print-codegen-error-header (errs) =
   let n = list-length errs
   in if n == 0 then print-line-uni ""
   else act
    print-line-uni ("CODEGEN-ERRORS:" & integer-to-text n)
    print-codegen-errors errs 0 n
   end

  print-bag-notices : DiagnosticBag -> [Console] Nothing
  print-bag-notices (bag) =
   print-notices-loop (bag.diagnostics) 0 (list-length (bag.diagnostics))

  print-notices-loop : List Diagnostic, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  print-notices-loop (ds) (i) (len) =
   if i == len then print-line-uni ""
   else let d = list-at ds i
   in if d.severity > sev-error then act
     print-line-uni (diagnostic-display d empty-file-table)
     print-notices-loop ds (i + 1) len
    end
    else print-notices-loop ds (i + 1) len

Section: Streaming Emission

  emit-streaming-ir-defs : List IRDef, List Text, List RenameEntry, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-streaming-ir-defs (ir-defs) (ctor-names) (renames) (i) (len) =
   if i == len then print-line-uni ""
   else let h = __heap-save
   in let text = codex-emit-def (list-at ir-defs i) ctor-names renames
   in act
    print-line-uni text
    let restored = __heap-restore h
    in emit-streaming-ir-defs ir-defs ctor-names renames (i + 1) len
   end

  emit-text-streaming : Text, CompileFlags -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-text-streaming (source) (flags) =
   let fe = compile-frontend source "Program" flags
   in let emit-deck = emit-build (list-length (fe.ir.defs) * 65536 + 8388608)
   in if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then act
    print-codegen-error-header (bag-errors (fe.bag))
    print-line-uni (format-heap-marks-wd (fe.heap-marks))
    print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED: errors in bag; no text emitted"
   end
   else let wd-marks = format-heap-marks-wd (fe.heap-marks) & format-phase-metrics-wd (fe.phase-metrics)
   in let ir-defs = fe.ir.defs
   in let len = list-length ir-defs
   in if len == 0
      then let header = if fe.text-meta.chapter-title == "" then ""
           else "Chapter: " & fe.text-meta.chapter-title & "\n"
             & codex-emit-grounds-line (fe.text-meta.ground-effects) & "\n"
             & if fe.text-meta.prose == "" then "" else " " & fe.text-meta.prose & "\n\n"
      in let type-defs-text = codex-emit-type-defs (fe.type-defs) 0
      in act
       print-line-uni wd-marks
       print-line-uni (header & type-defs-text)
      end
   else let h-emit = __heap-save
   in let header = if fe.text-meta.chapter-title == "" then ""
      else "Chapter: " & fe.text-meta.chapter-title & "\n"
        & codex-emit-grounds-line (fe.text-meta.ground-effects) & "\n"
        & if fe.text-meta.prose == "" then "" else " " & fe.text-meta.prose & "\n\n"
   in let type-defs-text = codex-emit-type-defs (fe.type-defs) 0
   in let first-text = codex-emit-def (list-at ir-defs 0) (fe.text-meta.ctor-names) (fe.renames)
   in act
    print-line-uni wd-marks
    print-line-uni (header & type-defs-text & first-text)
    let restored = __heap-restore h-emit
    in emit-streaming-ir-defs ir-defs (fe.text-meta.ctor-names) (fe.renames) 1 len
   end

Section: Entry Point

  emit-cdx : Text, Text, CompileFlags, Boolean -> [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing
  emit-cdx (source) (mode) (flags) (force-disk) =
   let exit-mode = if has-mode-flag mode "repl" then ExitRepl
    else if has-mode-flag mode "uefi" then ExitUefi
    else Exit
   in let want-map = has-mode-flag mode "map"
   in let want-disk = if force-disk then True else has-mode-flag mode "diskout"
   in let poison = has-mode-flag mode "poison"
   in let debug = has-mode-flag mode "debug"
   in let prof = has-mode-flag mode "profile"
   in let wd-mode = if has-mode-flag mode "pet" then WatchdogPet else WatchdogProgress
   in act
    if debug then print-line-uni ("DBG:frontend src=" & show (text-length source))
    else print-line-uni ""
    if prof then print-line-uni ("PROF-BEGIN: " & show (prof-start 0))
    else print-line-uni ""
    let fe = compile-frontend-cdx source "Codex_Codex" flags
    in act
     if debug then act
      print-line-uni ("DBG:emit defs=" & show (list-length (fe.cdx-ir.defs)))
      dbg-print-def-names (fe.cdx-ir.defs) 0 (list-length (fe.cdx-ir.defs))
     end
     else print-line-uni ""
     let result = compile-to-cdx-with-exit-mode fe exit-mode poison wd-mode
     in act
      if prof then print-line-uni ("PROF-END: " & show (prof-dump 0))
      else print-line-uni ""
      print-codegen-error-header (bag-errors (result.bag))
      print-bag-notices (result.bag)
      if want-map then emit-binary-tail-with-map result want-disk
      else emit-binary-tail result want-disk
     end
    end
   end

  emit-binary-size : EmitChapterResult -> Integer
  emit-binary-size (result) =
   list-length (result.header-bytes) + result.content-len + list-length (result.tail-bytes)

  disk-halted : Boolean -> [Console] Nothing
  disk-halted (to-disk) = act
   print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED: errors in bag; no binary emitted"
   disk-stop to-disk bp-orange
  end

  emit-binary-tail : EmitChapterResult, Boolean -> [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing
  emit-binary-tail (result) (to-disk) =
   if bag-has-errors (result.bag) then disk-halted to-disk
   else act
    print-line-uni ("SIZE:" & integer-to-text (emit-binary-size result))
    if to-disk then emit-binary-to-disk result
    else act
     write-binary (result.header-bytes)
     write-binary-buf (result.content-buf) 0 (result.content-len)
     write-binary (result.tail-bytes)
    end
   end

 write-binary and write-binary-buf reach a board through neither of their two
 arms: the fast one probes for codex-vm on port 0x511 and the fallback writes
 COM1 a byte at a time, and a UEFI machine with no UART answers neither. So a
 metal compile puts the CDX on the boot volume instead, and the verdict beside
 it, because print-line-uni is that same serial line.

 DISK mode takes this arm unconditionally, and emit-from-disk says so with an
 argument rather than emit-cdx re-deriving it from the mode line. Measured
 2026-08-09 with a probe at the head of emit-cdx: on that path `mode` is not a
 damaged string but not a string at all, arriving as twelve bytes of unrelated
 memory, so every has-mode-flag answers False and `parse-mode-cmd mode` does
 not equal "DISK" either. Deriving the sink from a value in that state is what
 made an earlier attempt dead code.

 The segments go down uncopied. The content is already a buffer, and routing it
 through a List would cost eight bytes of arena per byte of file.

  emit-binary-to-disk : EmitChapterResult -> [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  emit-binary-to-disk (result) = act
   disk-rung "compiled" 1 bp-blue bp-orange
   ok <- fat16-write-segments "OUT.CDX" (result.header-bytes) (result.content-buf) (result.content-len) (result.tail-bytes)
   emit-disk-verdict ok (emit-binary-size result)
  end

 The verdict re-reads the directory instead of taking the writer's word.
 Measured 2026-08-11: with the medium read-only, codex-vm printed
 `WARN: cannot reopen disk ... for write` on every sector and
 fat16-write-segments still answered True, so a rung that trusted `ok` was a
 rung that could not fail.

  disk-entry-size : Maybe Fat16DirEntry -> Integer
  disk-entry-size (m) = when m
    is Just (e) -> e.de-size
    is None -> 0 - 1

  disk-landed : Boolean, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  disk-landed (ok) (got) (want) =
    if got /= want then 0
    else if ok then 1
    else 0

  emit-disk-verdict : Boolean, Integer -> [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  emit-disk-verdict (ok) (size) = act
   vol <- fat16-boot-volume
   entry <- fat16-resolve-path vol "OUT.CDX"
   emit-disk-say (disk-landed ok (disk-entry-size entry) size) size (disk-entry-size entry)
  end

  emit-disk-say : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  emit-disk-say (landed) (size) (got) = act
   disk-mark "wrote" landed bp-white bp-blue
   let line = if landed == 1 then "OK OUT.CDX " & integer-to-text size else "FAILED " & integer-to-text got & " of " & integer-to-text size
   in act
    v <- fat16-write-file "OUT.TXT" line
    print-line-uni ("DISK-OUT: " & line)
    disk-stop True (if landed == 1 then bp-white else bp-blue)
   end
  end

  emit-binary-tail-with-map : EmitChapterResult, Boolean -> [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing
  emit-binary-tail-with-map (result) (to-disk) =
   if bag-has-errors (result.bag) then disk-halted to-disk
   else act
    print-line-uni ("SIZE:" & integer-to-text (emit-binary-size result))
    if to-disk then emit-binary-to-disk result
    else act
     write-binary (result.header-bytes)
     write-binary-buf (result.content-buf) 0 (result.content-len)
     write-binary (result.tail-bytes)
    end
    emit-symbol-map (result.symbol-map) 0 (list-length (result.symbol-map))
   end

  emit-symbol-map : List Text, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-symbol-map (lines) (i) (len) =
   if len == 0 then print-line-uni "MAP:0"
   else act
    print-line-uni ("MAP:" & show len)
    emit-map-lines lines i len
   end

  emit-map-lines : List Text, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-map-lines (lines) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then print-line-uni "MAP-END"
   else act
    print-line-uni (list-at lines i)
    emit-map-lines lines (i + 1) len
   end

  emit-text : CompileTarget, Text, CompileFlags -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-text (target) (source) (flags) =
   let fe = compile-frontend source "Program" flags
   in let h-pre-emit = __heap-save
   in let text = compile-text fe target
   in let h-post-emit = __heap-save
   in act
    print-codegen-error-header (bag-errors (fe.bag))
    if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED: errors in bag; no text emitted"
    else print-line-uni text
    print-line-uni ((format-heap-marks-wd (fe.heap-marks) & format-emit-marks h-pre-emit h-post-emit "WD:PHASE-"))
   end

  emit-ir-uni : Text, CompileFlags -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-ir-uni (source) (flags) =
   let fe = compile-frontend-ir source "Program" flags
   in let h-pre-emit = __heap-save
   in act
    print-codegen-error-header (bag-errors (fe.bag))
    print-bag-notices (fe.bag)
    if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED: errors in bag; no IR emitted"
    else act
     print-line-uni "IR-BEGIN"
     print-line-uni (emit-ir-chapter (ir-prune-unreachable (fe.ir) "opening") (fe.text-meta) (fe.type-defs))
     print-line-uni "IR-END"
    end
    let h-post-emit = __heap-save
    in print-line-uni ((format-heap-marks-wd (fe.heap-marks) & format-emit-marks h-pre-emit h-post-emit "WD:PHASE-"))
   end

 The SIZE-framed wire format the emit plugs consume: the SIZE line must
 precede the first payload byte, and the closing print-line supplies the
 one raw linefeed that follows the payload. Only emission knows a def's
 length, hence two passes -- ir-defs-wire-size for the total, then
 ir-print-defs through print-text so the wire bytes are exactly what
 emit-ir-chapter produced.

  emit-ir-cce : Text, CompileFlags -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-ir-cce (source) (flags) =
   let fe = compile-frontend-ir source "Program" flags
   in let h-pre-emit = __heap-save
   in act
    if flags.wire-trace then print-line-uni ("FE-DONE frontier " & integer-to-text h-pre-emit) else print-text ""
    print-codegen-error-header (bag-errors (fe.bag))
    if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED: errors in bag; no IR emitted"
    else let raw-defs = fe.ir.defs
     in act
      if flags.wire-trace then ir-trace-dce-cost raw-defs 0 (list-length raw-defs) else print-text ""
      let ir = ir-prune-unreachable (fe.ir) "opening"
      in let defs-len = list-length (ir.defs)
      in act
       if flags.wire-trace then ir-trace-def-sizes (ir.defs) 0 defs-len else print-text ""
       let prefix = emit-ir-chapter-prefix ir (fe.text-meta) (fe.type-defs)
       in let total = text-length prefix + ir-defs-wire-size (ir.defs) 0 defs-len 0 + 3
       in act
        print-line-uni ("SIZE:" & show total)
        print-text prefix
        ir-print-defs (ir.defs) 0 defs-len
        print-line ""
       end
      end
     end
    let h-post-emit = __heap-save
    in print-line-uni ((format-heap-marks-wd (fe.heap-marks) & format-emit-marks h-pre-emit h-post-emit "WD:PHASE-"))
   end

  emit-measure : Text, CompileFlags -> [Console] Nothing
  emit-measure (source) (flags) =
   let fe = compile-frontend source "Program" flags
   in let h-pre-emit = __heap-save
   in let text = compile-text fe CtCodexText
   in let h-post-emit = __heap-save
   in print-line-uni ((format-heap-marks (fe.heap-marks) & format-emit-marks h-pre-emit h-post-emit "PHASE-") & format-phase-decks (fe.phase-metrics) 0 (list-length (fe.phase-metrics)) "" & "EMIT-BYTES:" & integer-to-text (text-length text) & "\n")

  format-phase-decks : List PhaseMetrics, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  format-phase-decks (ms) (i) (len) (acc) =
   if i == len then acc
   else let m = list-at ms i
   in format-phase-decks ms (i + 1) len (acc & "DECK-" & integer-to-text i & ":phase=" & (m.label) & " origin=" & integer-to-text (m.deck-origin) & " end=" & integer-to-text (m.deck-end) & " used=" & integer-to-text (m.deck-end - m.deck-origin) & " bivy-origin=" & integer-to-text (m.bivy-origin) & " bivy-hwm=" & integer-to-text (m.bivy-hwm) & " bivy-used=" & integer-to-text (m.bivy-hwm - m.bivy-origin) & "\n")

  parse-mode-cmd : Text -> Text
  parse-mode-cmd (mode) =
   let parts = text-split mode " "
   in if list-length parts == 0 then mode
      else list-at parts 0

  mode-flag-value : Text, Text, Integer -> Integer
  mode-flag-value (mode) (prefix) (dflt) =
   let parts = text-split mode " "
   in mode-value-loop parts prefix (text-length prefix) 1 (list-length parts) dflt

  mode-value-loop : List Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  mode-value-loop (parts) (prefix) (plen) (i) (len) (dflt) =
   if i >= len then dflt
   else let p = list-at parts i
   in if text-starts-with p prefix
      then text-to-integer (substring p plen (text-length p - plen))
      else mode-value-loop parts prefix plen (i + 1) len dflt

  mode-flag-text : Text, Text -> Text
  mode-flag-text (mode) (prefix) =
   let parts = text-split mode " "
   in mode-text-loop parts prefix (text-length prefix) 1 (list-length parts)

  mode-text-loop : List Text, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  mode-text-loop (parts) (prefix) (plen) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then ""
   else let p = list-at parts i
   in if text-starts-with p prefix
      then substring p plen (text-length p - plen)
      else mode-text-loop parts prefix plen (i + 1) len

  has-mode-flag : Text, Text -> Boolean
  has-mode-flag (mode) (flag) =
   let parts = text-split mode " "
   in has-flag-loop parts flag 1 (list-length parts)

  has-flag-loop : List Text, Text, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  has-flag-loop (parts) (flag) (i) (len) =
   if i >= len then False
   else if list-at parts i == flag then True
   else has-flag-loop parts flag (i + 1) len

  dbg-print-def-names : List IRDef, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  dbg-print-def-names (defs) (i) (len) = act
   if i >= len then print-line-uni ""
   else let d = list-at defs i
   in act
    print-line-uni ("DBG:def " & show i & " " & d.name)
    dbg-print-def-names defs (i + 1) len
   end
  end

  parse-mode-flags : Text, Integer -> CompileFlags
  parse-mode-flags (mode) (unit-len) =
   CompileFlags { prose = has-mode-flag mode "prose", escape-check = has-mode-flag mode "escape-check", poison-compact = has-mode-flag mode "poison-compact", deck-scale = effective-deck-scale mode unit-len, phase-trace = has-mode-flag mode "debug", wire-trace = has-mode-flag mode "wsz", pipeline = pipeline-of mode }

 The volume is resolved from the disk's own GPT rather than assumed to
 start at LBA 2048. That constant is only right for an image our own
 GptWriter laid down; a stick partitioned elsewhere puts the volume at a
 different offset. 2048 remains the fallback when there is no readable GPT.

  emit-from-disk : Text -> [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  emit-from-disk (mode) = act
   disk-rung "mode" 1 bp-yellow bp-cyan
   path-result <- read-line
   vol <- fat16-boot-volume
   disk-rung "volume" (bp-truth (vol.vol-bytes-per-sector == 512)) bp-magenta bp-yellow
   when path-result
    is Just (path) ->
      when fat16-read-text vol path
        is Just (source) ->
          let o = bp-pass 1 bp-orange bp-magenta
          in let foreword-prefix = disk-resolve-forewords vol source mode
          in let full = foreword-prefix & source
          in let flags = parse-mode-flags mode (text-length full)
          in emit-cdx full mode flags True
        is None -> disk-no-source ("DISK: file not found: " & path)
    is None -> disk-no-source "DISK: no path on stdin"
  end

 The volume rung reads the BPB rather than the mount's own answer.
 fat16-boot-volume returns a record whatever the medium said, so a payload
 built without UEFI mode reads down the bare-metal path, gets zeroes, and
 mounts a volume that satisfies every pointer test.

 The source rung paints on the way through and does not trace, because
 `mode` is intact in this frame and damaged one call deeper. The next rung's
 line names it: nothing reaches `compiled` without ORANGE having been painted.

  disk-no-source : Text -> [Console] Nothing
  disk-no-source (why) = act
   disk-rung "source" 0 bp-orange bp-magenta
   print-line-uni why
  end

  compile-plain : Text, Text, Text, CompileFlags -> [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  compile-plain (source) (cmd) (mode) (flags) =
   if cmd == "CDX" then emit-cdx source mode flags (has-mode-flag mode "diskout")
   else if cmd == "IR-UNI" then emit-ir-uni source flags
   else if cmd == "IR-CCE" then emit-ir-cce source flags
   else if cmd == "MEASURE" then emit-measure source flags
   else emit-text-streaming source flags

  compile-with-quotations : SourceSplit, Text, Text, CompileFlags -> [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing
  compile-with-quotations (split) (cmd) (mode) (flags) =
   let mountain = init-phase-allocator
   in let keep-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-quote-keep-floor 0
   in let keep-base = build keep-height
   in let scratch-height = scaled-floor (flags.deck-scale) demand-quote-scratch-floor 0
   in let scratch-base = build scratch-height
   in let base-ws = build-works (split.sp-works)
   in let base-bundle = base-ws.ws-bundle
   in act
    bundle <- if has-mode-flag mode "store" then store-read-bundle base-bundle else act base-bundle end
    let qr = resolve-quotations (split.sp-body) bundle
    in if bag-has-errors (qr.qr-bag)
       then refuse-quotations (bag-errors (qr.qr-bag))
       else admit-quotations split cmd mode flags keep-base keep-height (qr.qr-prefix)
   end

  refuse-quotations : List Diagnostic -> [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  refuse-quotations (errs) = act
   print-codegen-error-header errs
   print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED: quotation refused; nothing emitted"
  end

  admit-quotations : SourceSplit, Text, Text, CompileFlags, Integer, Integer, Text -> [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  admit-quotations (split) (cmd) (mode) (flags) (keep-base) (keep-height) (prefix) =
   if check-deck-overflow (text-length prefix * 2 + 4096) keep-height == 1
   then refuse-quotations (bag-errors (deck-overflow-bag "QUOTE-KEEP"))
   else let dset = __deck-set keep-base
   in let kept = deck-record (copy-sx-text keep-base prefix)
   in let sealed = compact-phase flags poison-parse
   in compile-plain (kept & split.sp-body) cmd mode flags

  dispatch-on-mode : Text -> [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing
  dispatch-on-mode (mode) = act
   let cmd = parse-mode-cmd mode
   in if cmd == "DISK" then emit-from-disk mode
   else act
    source-raw <- read-file-uni mode
    let raw = utf8-to-cce source-raw
    in let split = split-quoted-works raw
    in let flags = parse-mode-flags mode (text-length raw)
    in if has-quotations (split.sp-body)
       then compile-with-quotations split cmd mode flags
       else compile-plain (split.sp-body) cmd mode flags
   end
  end

  opening : [Console, FileSystem, Device.Block] Nothing = act
   disk-rung "entered" 1 bp-cyan bp-red
   mode-result <- read-line
   when mode-result
    is Just (mode) -> dispatch-on-mode mode
    is None -> disk-no-mode 0
  end

  disk-no-mode : Integer -> [Console] Nothing
  disk-no-mode (dummy) = act
   disk-rung "mode" 0 bp-yellow bp-cyan
   print-line-uni "Codex: no input mode on stdin"
  end

